WeSpeaker ECAPA-TDNN512 (voxceleb_ECAPA512.onnx)
  https://huggingface.co/Wespeaker/wespeaker-voxceleb-ecapa-tdnn512
  Trained with WeSpeaker, https://github.com/wenet-e2e/wespeaker (code: Apache-2.0).
  License: CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). The model card
  has no license field; WeSpeaker states that pretrained models follow the license
  of their training data, and VoxCeleb is CC BY 4.0.
  Training data: VoxCeleb (Nagrani, Chung, Xie, Zisserman),
  https://www.robots.ox.ac.uk/~vgg/data/voxceleb/

pyannote segmentation-3.0 (segmentation.onnx)
  pyannote segmentation-3.0 powerset model, ONNX export by onnx-community.
  https://huggingface.co/onnx-community/pyannote-segmentation-3.0
  License: MIT.

faster-whisper 1.2.1 and CTranslate2 4.9.0 (speech-to-text for en de fr es it nl pl; optional `asr` extra)
  https://github.com/SYSTRAN/faster-whisper
  https://github.com/OpenNMT/CTranslate2
  License: MIT.
  Also installed by the `recap` extra. Not imported unless a start actually transcribes.
  Weights are OpenAI Whisper small, converted by Systran (MIT), downloaded from a pinned
  commit and checked against the SHA-256 of model.bin. They are not fetched from a branch.
  English: https://huggingface.co/Systran/faster-whisper-small.en
    revision d1d751a5f8271d482d14ca55d9e2deeebbae577f
    model.bin 483545366 bytes, sha256 62b2a45b05ee59acb4a5341b33ee35e041395d378d418a18acfe4c9e768ee37a
  de fr es it nl pl: https://huggingface.co/Systran/faster-whisper-small
    revision 536b0662742c02347bc0e980a01041f333bce120
    model.bin 483546902 bytes, sha256 3e305921506d8872816023e4c273e75d2419fb89b24da97b4fe7bce14170d671
  Inference is CPU int8. Podcue does not send a Hugging Face token.

Moonshine (ja, ko, zh only; optional `moonshine` extra)
  Downloaded by the moonshine-voice package. The non-English Moonshine models are
  released under the non-commercial Moonshine Community License:
  https://www.moonshine.ai/license
  Those terms apply only when podcue runs with --language ja, ko or zh. No other
  language is routed to Moonshine. The recap extra does not use Moonshine.

Recap extra (`podcue[recap]`): Kokoro narration, soundfile, and yt-dlp.
  These are not installed by a plain `podcue` install. Commercial use is allowed
  for each direct dependency below. Two transitive packages are GPL-3.0-or-later;
  distributing a combined work that links them carries GPL-3 obligations. podcue
  does not vendor them.

kokoro 0.9.4 (narration; Python >=3.10, <3.13)
  https://github.com/hexgrad/kokoro
  License: Apache-2.0.
  Voices and weights: hexgrad/Kokoro-82M, Apache-2.0,
  https://huggingface.co/hexgrad/Kokoro-82M
  Downloaded on first narration into the Hugging Face cache. Not part of this package.
  Training audio under CC BY, used for a few hours of Kokoro v1.0: Koniwa `tnc`
  (CC BY 3.0, under 1 hour) and SIWIS (CC BY 4.0, under 11 hours). See the model card.
  English grapheme-to-phoneme loads spaCy en_core_web_sm 3.8.0 (MIT). That model is
  not on PyPI. podcue downloads the pinned wheel and checks its SHA-256:
  https://github.com/explosion/spacy-models/releases/download/en_core_web_sm-3.8.0/en_core_web_sm-3.8.0-py3-none-any.whl
  sha256 1932429db727d4bff3deed6b34cfc05df17794f4a52eeb26cf8928f7c1a0fb85

misaki 0.9.4, extra `en` (grapheme-to-phoneme, required by kokoro)
  https://github.com/hexgrad/misaki
  License: Apache-2.0.
  The `en` extra also installs:
  phonemizer-fork (GPL-3.0-or-later), https://pypi.org/project/phonemizer-fork/
  espeakng-loader, https://pypi.org/project/espeakng-loader/
    The loader's package metadata declares no license. It redistributes the
    espeak-ng shared library, which is GPL-3.0-or-later:
    https://github.com/espeak-ng/espeak-ng/blob/master/COPYING
  num2words (LGPL), https://github.com/savoirfairelinux/num2words
  English narration tries espeak only for out-of-dictionary words and continues
  if that fallback does not load.
  torch (BSD-3-Clause) and transformers (Apache-2.0) are pulled in by kokoro.

soundfile 0.14.0
  https://github.com/bastibe/python-soundfile
  License: BSD-3-Clause.
  Wheels bundle libsndfile, LGPL-2.1 or LGPL-3.0, loaded as a shared library:
  https://github.com/libsndfile/libsndfile

